e world from the pirates and other  criminals who are yeah the bad guys but  since the heroes of our stories are  pirates we soon discover that the world  is not simply black and white early on  in the story Luffy liberate Zorro from  the hands of Captain Morgan to the  surprise of everyone the Marine  stationed at the base all thanked Luffy  for liberating them as well from the  tyranny of their captain and with that  Oda showed us from pretty early on in  the story that his world is morally  the lines between good and bad are very  fluent not only in the groups like the  Pirates or the Marines but often also in  individuals themselves a great example  for this is Robin who is capable of  immoral and violent behavior and is also  introduced as an antagonist to Luffy and  his crew only after learning her story  and her unexpected joining of the crew  do we start to see her as a person with  a good heart and over time Robin has  become one of the most popular and loved  characters in one piece this concept is  what makes the characters in the story  so incredibly complex and interesting  another story that has built its success  on this way of character designs well is  Game of Thrones  where there is no pure good or evil in  the characters and where justice is also  presented as a concept that does not  have a clear definition now when we look  back at one piece many of the Pirates  actually fit in this black and white  mentality way of thinking since they  truly are nothing more than criminals  but you have to keep in mind that there  are at least as many who turned towards  the pirate life for very different  reasons a bad standard of living revenge  a dream or simply the wish for freedom  are the motivations for many pirates  including the straw hats and along the  road we meet many people who will be  considered nothing more than criminals  in the eye of the world government that  we actually get to know as the good guys  this includes pirates outcasts and the  