d individual situations  into account when passing judgment he  decided to let rob and go from a Hara  and was happy to see her becoming part  of destroyed crew by showing mercy  compassion and respect towards enemies  that have earned it in his eyes  inevitably he eventually clashed with a  canoe due to the incredibly different  views on justice these different ideas  of Justice showed just how in  homogeneous even the Marines are so why  is the concept of justice that the world  government proclaims for themselves so  hypocritical the answer to that lies in  the way that this so-called justice is  executed in the Wimpy's world the  failure to comply with the idea of  justice by the different law-enforcement  factions of the government is a common  theme in the story in the end their  actions are often considered as equally  bad or even worse than those of the  Pirates they actually target trampling  on the rights and needs of civilians in  order to pursue an agenda such actions  by the Marines include everything from  corrupt officers like Morgan to the  killing of civilians on ohhara by Aquino  one of the most gruesome acts committed  by the Marines in the story was the  slaughter of numerous children and women  in the search for Rajas child the  killing of innocents justified by the  danger of a baby of a criminal that  doesn't really sound like any justice to  me another faction executing justice in  the name of the world government are the  cipher pol agencies  RUP Lucci is famously and repeatedly  shown to only embrace justice as a form  of indication for living out his  bloodlust and cruelty  he puts murder and pain before capture  and pushes the boundaries of bringing  people to justice towards cold-blooded  murder  despite the views that all Pirates are  evil the world government also  introduced a system of the Warlord's  these Pirates are pardoned for all their  past crimes and those that the crewmates  committed and are to a certain extent  even allowed to keep committing more the  government is so to speak willing to  overlook certain things in order to gain  more control and maintained a hold on  society's faith in the strength of  justice the law system itself is down to  its core as far from just as it's  possible judges exist in the one-piece  world but as we saw with robin's trial  they are only for show and hold no real  chance for a fair process as a part of  that the prison of impel down is  designed to prevent any captives from  leaving the place alive even those  without a life sentence die in prison  from a systematic torture they're  sentenced to something that the jailers  find great pleasure in doing the whole  place goes against the very idea of a  real prison keeping criminals with a  life sentence away from society and  making those who did not fit to be  reintegrated into society for a second  chance only in one piece the system does  really not allow any second chances but  the final and maybe worst argument for  the hypocrisy of the world government is  the concept of the world Nobles the fact  that this elite group is accepted from  any moral judgment and even practice  active slavery coz in its essence  against the very idea of justice itself  since you cannot simply exclude someone  from this idea the world Nobles are  allowed to murder rape or anything they  please without being part of a kind  whose absolute justice additionally by  owning most of the wealth in the world  they are also the reason many people  resort to the life of a pirate in the  first place so how can it be that  despite all those atrocities committed  by all sides the Marines are perceived  as righteous and good while the Pirates  and revolutionaries are generally seen  as bad and cruel the best answer to this  question might come from one of the last  people he would expect donki hote  doflamingo has the following words  regarding justice pirates are evil the  Marines are righteous  these terms have always changed  throughout the course of history kids  who have never seen piece and kids who  have never seen war have different  values those who stand at the top  determined what's wrong and what's right  this very place is neutral ground and  justice will prevail you say but of  course it will whoever wins this war  becomes justice so in the world of one  piece the world government has been in  power since the void century and  therefore shape the views on who and  what is right for centuries being  nothing else than an undemocratic regime  with the unknown but nonetheless single  ruler and a royal class that is free  from any moral illegal boundaries  justice against the proclaimed enemy is  nothing more than a tool of propaganda  that hides the injustice of the system  since this regime has been in existence  for such a long time this belief of the  government being the ultimate good and  just entity in the world has sunk in  with large parts of the population that  actually carries this system so you  might wonder what can be done about this  and the simple answer to that is that in  essence this is what Luffy's journey is  going to be all about in the end because  even though the revolutionaries are  invading Marysia right now we can assume  that the final role of liberating the  world will be fulfilled by Luffy since  his ultimate goal is to be free so now  incredibly curious about what you guys  think about the concept of justice in  one piece share your thoughts in the  comments below  if you like this video leave me a thumbs  up and please subscribe to my channel to  be notified for any future content of  mine I hope to see you guys around next  time and until then have a great week  [Music]  you

